Source: creature-cli
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: April White <april@creature.engineering>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/opsnlops/creature-console

Package: creature-cli
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Command-line client for Creature Server
 A CLI for interacting with the Creature API server to control animatronic creatures.

Package: creature-mqtt
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: MQTT bridge for Creature Server events
 Bridges Creature websocket events into MQTT topics for Home Assistant and automation stacks.

Package: creature-agent
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: OpenAI MQTT agent for Creature Server
 Consumes MQTT alerts, generates responses with OpenAI, and schedules ad-hoc speech animations.

Package: creature-world
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Authoritative shared-world simulator for Creature clients
 Runs the Creature World HTTP service, which maintains the authoritative shared-world
 state used by Creature clients and integrations.

Package: creature-communicator-gateway
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Narrow synchronization gateway for Beaky Communicator
 Runs the independently deployed HTTP gateway for Beaky Communicator client
 synchronization, foreground leases, and future notification delivery.

Package: creature-house
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Home Assistant adapter for Beaky's Virtual World
 Follows Home Assistant and tells Creature World what the house sees (doors,
 motion, people, temperatures, camera detections) and sets lighting scenes when
 a character is asked to. The token lives in /etc/default/creature-house.
